 What is The best practices in http adapter ?
 A.Always use HTTPS
   ➔ Never use HTTP. Always encrypt communication.

   Use Authentication
   ➔ Set Basic Auth, OAuth2, or Certificates.
   ➔ Never leave it open.

   Enable CSRF Protection (for POST, PUT, DELETE)
   ➔ Protects from attack if someone misuses your endpoint.

   Set Correct HTTP Method
   ➔ Use GET for read, POST for create, PUT for update, DELETE for delete.

   Set Proper Timeouts
   ➔ Avoid long waiting by setting smart timeout values.

   Handle Errors
   ➔ Always add Exception Subprocess to manage failures nicely.

   Secure Credentials
   ➔ Store passwords and tokens in "Security Material", not inside iFlow.

   Set Content-Type Header
   ➔ Example: application/json or application/xml.
   ➔ Always tell the receiver what format you're sending.

   Limit Logging
   ➔ Don’t log passwords, tokens, or personal data.

   Use IP Whitelisting (if possible)
   ➔ Only allow trusted IPs to call your HTTPS endpoint.
